    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-75">Per D-75 (with ontology-r1, 2026-10-15): the core record of an invoice line (sprk_billingevent) is derived only from the line's OWN core-record lookup (sprk_matter / sprk_project / sprk_regardingworkassignment, FR-05), never by walking sprk_billingevent.sprk_invoice; a line may in future not belong to exactly one invoice. Any other derivation needs uac-r2 approval (STOP and ask). The line subject is registered in SecureChildLineage and the census (ontology-r1 condition) so secure-family placement works for line-subject Signals and Decision Records.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Existing dedupe keys do not change: BuildDedupeKey keeps its inputs and format; a line subject only adds keys whose subject segment is sprk_billingevent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The lookup is added only through TodoRegardingBuilder.SignalAndDecisionRecordRegardingLookupByEntity; no second map is created in SignalWriter or DecisionRecordWriter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Core derivation for invoice and line subjects comes only from CoreAncestorResolver.ResolveStampsAsync (task 013's extension); SignalWriter does not walk lookups itself.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Ontology-owned files (Services/Signals/**) and uac-r2 tables (CoreAncestorResolver, SecureChildLineage, census tests) change only as listed; the PR records ontology-r1 and uac-r2 reviews. Run /conflict-check before the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Schema script runs only against spaarkedev1, additive, -WhatIf supported, entity-scoped PublishXml. Solution source: export with scripts/solution-authoring/Export-SpaarkeMasterSource.ps1 to a temp folder and copy only the sprk_Signal, sprk_DecisionRecord and relationship files that change; no version bump.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions.md">Publish-size delta against a fresh master build recorded; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">The new lookup is one more entity-specific lookup of the existing pair; at most one subject lookup per row stays enforced by the builder's guard.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-94">D-94 (uac-r2 approval of option A): make sprk_billingevent an intermediate in CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns with root columns exactly sprk_project, sprk_matter, sprk_regardingworkassignment (never sprk_invoice or sprk_timekeeper; sprk_timekeeper stays a Party), in lockstep with the TypeScript INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS row in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts (same three columns, same order) and RecordContainerResolver.ChildAncestorLinks (KindByEntity / ByEntity follow exactly those three). ChildRecordEntities, CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES and StampedOutsideAccessTaxonomy stay unchanged. These three files are added to this task's scope by D-94.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-94">D-94 condition 1: confirm the three lookup column names and targets on sprk_billingevent by a read-only spaarkedev1 metadata read, and cite it in the IntermediateRootColumns comment like the other rows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-94">D-94 condition 2: every write path that changes one of the three columns on a line runs the restamp for the line's dependants (as the other intermediates do), and the reconciliation job covers sprk_billingevent as a source; verify the StampSourceColumns entries for sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord (sprk_regardinginvoiceline -&gt; sprk_billingevent) are what both the restamper and the reconciler read. If no BFF path edits a line's core lookup today, say so in the notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-94">D-94 condition 3 tests: must-fire, a line whose sprk_invoice names an invoice under a different matter still resolves the line's own root; must-fire, a line whose root columns name different records is a derivation error (nothing stamped, writers refuse); a line with no core lookup is NoAncestor and SignalWriter and DecisionRecordWriter refuse it (pin the refusal); StampSourceTopology_IsClosed, IntermediateRootColumns_MatchTheTypeScriptSide and IntermediateRootColumns_MatchTheResolversFollowedRoots pass.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-94">D-94 condition 4 tests: a document or to-do regarding a line of a SECURE matter resolves to the secure matter's container; a line with conflicting root columns is refused and never given a default container.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-94">D-94 condition 5: run the targeted jest suite for PolymorphicResolverService.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-94">D-94 review gate: uac-r2 reviews the diff (three tables, restamp coverage, tests) before merge; the main session sends it. ontology-r1 still reviews the ontology-owned files.</constraint>
  </constraints>

